From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:52:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] J714s release 8: kernel v272-12 (lid sleep, s2idle) and
 firmware j714s13 (one boot guard for every M5 board)

Re-pinned from betizzel/omarchy-m5 9b74652: linux-aurora
7.3.0.aurora17.v272-12 (d2dcbe31..., 44289449 bytes): aurora-silicon/linux
integration/aurora c0a2a752 plus patches/j714s-27.2/linux 0001-0032
(v272-11 rebased, with the J714s suspend-to-idle stack: Jens Axboe's
#1647, Isaac-Duarte's #2012 and #2018; four patches now upstream dropped).
Deep sleep stays off (CONFIG_APPLE_SOC_SLEEP not set): mem_sleep offers
s2idle only. The qualification pins follow 7.3.0-17.v272-12-ARCH.

omarchy-aurora-firmware 20261014.j714s13 (af8a8d00..., 55533 bytes) from
82d914e (chrisohearn's betizzel/omarchy-m5#16): the j714s12 boot guard as
m5-boot-guard for every M5 board, the board read from the device tree.
Nothing else changes. Set j714s-dev-runtime-fd29d86c50ef.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
